# XSH getgid()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.getgid.001
anchor     functions/getgid.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/getgid.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       getgid() returns the real group ID: the number the id utility
           prints for "id -g -r" in the same process environment (read
           through popen()).
note       The id utility is the standard's own second source for the
           value; the test is UNRESOLVED if its output is not one decimal
           number.
test       t/001-matches-id.c

assertion  XSH.getgid.002
anchor     functions/getgid.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/getgid.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       In a child of a privileged test, after setegid(65534) getgid()
           still returns 0, and after setgid(65534) (with privileges, all
           three group IDs) it returns 65534.
needs      root
note       The IDs are set in the setup phase with setegid() and setgid();
           the child is UNRESOLVED when the system does not let it make
           those changes.
test       t/002-real.c

assertion  XSH.getgid.003
anchor     functions/getgid.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       getgid() leaves errno as it was (two different values tried).
test       t/003-errno.c
